                <pb facs="0749" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">671.116/49: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Owsley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-22T17:00:00-05:00">March 22, 1935—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Your 3, March 2, 4 p.m. Please telegraph whether suspension of authorizations
                    for importation of American merchandise still obtains and date on which action
                    was taken on the Department’s telegram No. 1 March 11, 5 p.m. Also report any
                    information you may have as to the Rumanian Government’s reaction to your note
                    and as to when a reply may be expected.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
